  "decision_summary": "Keep low (F < 20%). L6 hepatic-clearance and metabolic-stability records show that steroid substrates undergo CYP3A-mediated hepatic metabolism with measurable clearance, mechanistically supporting first-pass hepatic loss for this lipophilic corticosteroid acetal-ester prodrug. The evidence is indirect and for other steroids, so it does not change the prediction; the low direction remains supported by transferable human low-F contexts, very low oral exposure of ester corticosteroid prodrugs, and low aqueous solubility."
}

